-- title:
--   Logarithmic supersingular polar differentials lie in the image of Theta₀
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $p \neq 2$ is a prime, $M$ is a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ is a subgroup containing, by `hHp`, every unit whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is $1$; $S$ is a set of natural numbers. The hypothesis `hin` is the predicate `HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H`: for every prime $\ell$ the condition `HeckeInputsHAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) M H ℓ` holds, and for every $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ there is an automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d`. Write $J_H =$ `JH M H` for the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of degree-zero divisor classes of the field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $T =$ [`TateModule p (JH M H)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) for the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_H$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$.
--
--   *Hecke algebra data.* $\mathbb{T}$ is a commutative ring and a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra acting on $T$ compatibly with the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-action (scalar tower); `hfaith` says the action of $\mathbb{T}$ on $T$ is faithful. A map `op` sends each element of the generator type [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) (constructors $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid M$, $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, and $\langle d\rangle$ for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$) to $\mathbb{T}$, with `hop`: $\mathrm{op}(g)$ acts on $T$ as `tateGenOpH M H S p g`, the endomorphism of the Tate module induced by `genOpH M H S g`; `hgen`: the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{T}$ generated by the range of `op` is everything. Further, `S'` is an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) of $\mathbb{T}$ (a finite family of idempotents `S'.e` that is completely orthogonal, a family of maximal ideals `S'.𝔪` exhausting all maximal ideals, with `S'.e i ∈ S'.𝔪 j` precisely for $i \neq j$), $i_0$ is an index of that family, and `hord` requires $\mathrm{op}(U_p) \notin$ `S'.𝔪 i₀`.
--
--   *The place and the inertia-fixed corner.* `Pl` is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `hPl`: $p$ lies in its nonunits; its residue field has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed. `P0` is a $\mathbb{T}$-submodule of $T$, characterised by `hP0` as the set of $x$ lying both in the corner submodule [`IharaLemma.cornerSubmodule (S'.e i₀)`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L46) (the image of multiplication by `S'.e i₀`) and in the subspace on which every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of `Pl` over $\mathbb{Q}$ acts through `JH.tateGaloisRep` by the scalar `cyclotomicCharacter` $(\sigma) \in \mathbb{Z}_p^\times$.
--
--   *The mod-$p$ differentials.* $K$ is an algebraically closed field which is an algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ and over the residue field of `Pl`. Set $\Gamma' =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), where `infSubgroup` is the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$, and let $\Omega_{\mathrm{ss}} =$ `ssPolarDifferentials K Γ' p`, the $K$-submodule of $\Omega[\,$`qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ'`$\,\!/K]$ consisting of those differentials that are regular at every place outside `ssPlacesQExp K Γ' p` (the places cut out by `IsSSPlaceQExp`) and have at most a simple pole at each place in that set. A ring homomorphism $\tau$ from $\mathbb{T}$ to $\mathrm{End}_K(\Omega_{\mathrm{ss}})$ is given, with `hτ`: for each generator $g$, $\tau(\mathrm{op}(g))$ acts on $\Omega_{\mathrm{ss}}$ as `genDiffModL K p M H hpM S g` (Hecke operators at $T_\ell$ and at $U_q$ for $q \neq p$, the Frobenius pushforward at $U_p$, the diamond action at $\langle d \rangle$).
--
--   *Integral model, Néron object, Abel–Jacobi.* `hj` states $j \in$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`; $\mathfrak{X}$ is an `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` and $\Lambda$ a `JHNeronObjectAtP.LevelData p M H hpM Pl`. The hypothesis `hrepΛ` asserts that the designation built from $\Lambda$ represents the relative sub-Picard functor for `toBase p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` cut out by `algEquivZeroCut`; $O$ is a `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM Pl hPl Λ`; `hD` and `hDQ` assert the corresponding representability for the designation built from $O$ over `R p` and after base change to $\mathbb{Q}$, and `hsep` the separatedness of that base change. The data `ajQ`, `kQ`, `ajbar`, `εbar` are the Abel–Jacobi morphism over $\mathbb{Q}$, a comparison of pullbacks, its induced map on $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ and a base point; the hypotheses `hpoinc`, `hajQε`, `hajQ`, `hkQ₁`, `hkQ₂`, `hajbar`, `hajbar_over`, `hεbar`, `hεbar_aj` (summarised here) identify the Poincaré bundles before and after base change, pin down `ajQ` on the zero section and on arbitrary field-valued points through the line bundle of a point tensored with the ideal module of the section, and fix the compatibilities of `kQ`, `ajbar` and `εbar`. Finally `hpts_law` says that `O.pts` is additive for the relative group law attached to `hD`, and `hAJ` says that for any two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ with $s$ compatible with the section $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ there is a degree-zero divisor $Dv$ equal to $(x) - (s)$ under `pointEquivPlace` whose class satisfies $(O.\mathrm{pts}(\,[Dv]\,))_1 = x \cdot \mathrm{ajbar}$.
--
--   *The henselian base.* $R$ is a domain and a henselian local ring with algebraically closed residue field, an $R$-algebra structure on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ being given faithfully, such that: `hRA` the image of $R$ lies in `Pl`; `hRdvr` $R$ is a discrete valuation ring; `hRirr` $p$ is irreducible in $R$; `hRfix` the inertia subgroup of `Pl` over $\mathbb{Q}$ consists exactly of the automorphisms fixing the image of $R$ pointwise; `hRmax` every element of `Pl` fixed by that inertia subgroup comes from $R$.
--
--   *$p$-divisible groups.* $\mathcal{G}$ is a [`PDivisibleGroup R p h`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199) (levels `𝒢.level v`, finite free Hopf $R$-algebras of rank $p^{vh}$, with surjective transition maps whose kernels are the $p^v$-torsion ideals), and $\Delta$ an injective additive map from $\mathcal{G}$-points over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to $J_H$, with `hΔlev`: `O.finPts (p ^ v)` is exactly the image under $\Delta$ of the level-$v$ points; `hΔgal`: $\Delta$ is equivariant for automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ that are $R$-linear; `hΔhecke`: each generator $g$ is realised by a family of coalgebra endomorphisms $\varphi$ of the levels, compatible with the transition maps, inducing `genOpH M H S g` through $\Delta$. Further $\mathcal{B}$ is a [`PDivisibleGroup R p hB`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199) with coalgebra maps $\psi_v : \mathcal{B}.\mathrm{level}\,v \to \mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v$, and: `hhB`: $h = O.\mathrm{toricRank} + h_B$; `hhB2`: $h_B = 2h'$; `hψt`: compatibility of $\psi$ with transitions; `hψker`: a level-$v$ point of $\mathcal{G}$ has trivial image in $\mathcal{B}$ precisely when its $\Delta$-image lies in `O.toricPts (p ^ v)`; `hψsurj`: every level-$v$ point of $\mathcal{B}$ is such an image; `hψred`: if the image in $\mathcal{B}$ of a point reduces to the identity (all values of the corresponding algebra map differ from the counit by an element of `Pl`-valuation $< 1$), then so does the point itself; `hperiod`: for $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup, $z$ a $p^v$-torsion class of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ and $y$ a level-$v$ point with $\Delta y = \sigma \cdot z - z$, the image of $y$ in $\mathcal{B}$ reduces to the identity in this sense.
--
--   *Realisation on the Néron object.* $\rho_h :$ `R p` $\to R$ and morphisms $\iota_v : \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v) \to O.G$ are given with: `hρh` compatibility of $\rho_h$ with the structure maps to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; `hιbase` the base compatibility of $\iota_v$; `hιcl` the induced morphism to the fibre product is a closed immersion; `hιp` $\iota_v$ is killed by multiplication by $p^v$; `hιpts` $O.\mathrm{pts}(\Delta(\cdot))$ factors through $\iota_v$ along the algebra map of the point; `hιmul` $\iota_v$ transports the group law on points of $\mathcal{G}$ into the multiplication $O.L.\mathrm{mul}$; `hιt` compatibility with the transition maps; `hιhecke` each generator is realised by a family $\varphi$ of level endomorphisms compatible with transitions, with $O.\mathrm{hecke}\,S\,g$ through $\iota$, and with `genOpH` through $\Delta$; `hιfin` the comparison morphism $j_v$ into the $p^v$-kernel pulled back to $R$ is an open and a closed immersion whose image contains every point lying over the closed point of $R$.
--
--   *Atkin–Lehner, sections, specialisation, degeneracy.* `wgen` is a semilinear automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `hwgen`: it computes the effect of $\mathfrak{X}.w$ on places via `pointEquivPlace`; $\rho :$ `R p` $\to$ `Pl` with `hρ` and `hσA` identifies $\Lambda.\sigma_A$ with $\operatorname{Spec}\rho$. The hypotheses `hsp` and `hspΛ` (long binder lists, summarised here) assert, for each $i \in \{0,1\}$ and each configuration of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $y_1, y_2$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$, lifts $u_1, u_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\rho$ (in `hsp` with image in the smooth locus), residue-field points $u_{\kappa,1}, u_{\kappa,2}$ of the fibre, closed points $P_1, P_2$ respectively $Q_1, Q_2$ of the fibre curve model over them, and a degree-zero divisor $Dv = (y_1) - (y_2)$, the existence of a section $s$ of $O.g$ (respectively $s_0$ of $\Lambda.f$) over $\Lambda.\sigma_A$ realising the Abel–Jacobi image of $[Dv]$ (respectively of $O.\mathrm{degPts}\,i\,[Dv]$) and specialising, under $O.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ (respectively $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$), to the prescribed glued $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ datum $x$ supported on the $i$-th component (respectively to the class of the divisor $(Q_1) - (Q_2)$). `hdia0` asserts that each $e \in (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ acts on closed points of the fibre curve model compatibly with `diamondActionModL` on places. A unit $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ is given with `hd`: its image in $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ equals $p$, and `hdH`: the image of $d$ or of $-d$ lies in `infSubgroup p M H hpM`; also $M/p \neq 0$. Endomorphisms $F, F^{-1}, F^{*}$ of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the fibre function field are given with `hF`: $F$ is `qExpFrobeniusPushforwardModL`; `hFinv`: $F$ and $F^{-1}$ are mutually inverse; `hFstar`: $F^{*} = p \cdot F^{-1}$. A unit `pb` reducing to $p$ and the diamond endomorphism $\delta$ it induces are given with `hδ`. The degeneracy data consist of $\alpha_i :$ `JH (M/p) (infSubgroup …)` $\to J_H$ and sections `degPull i` of $O.g$ over $\Lambda.f$ for $i \in \{0,1\}$, with `hpull`: $O.\mathrm{pts}(\alpha_i x) = \Lambda.\mathrm{pts}(x)$ followed by `degPull i`; `hpullsp`: on specialisations, `degPull 0` induces $(z, F^{*}z)$ and `degPull 1` induces $(F^{*}z, \delta z)$; `hpull_mul`: each `degPull i` is compatible with the group laws. Finally `Wbar` is the endomorphism of $J_H$ given by the action of `wgen` (`hWbar`), and `hUPgen` states $\mathrm{genOpH}(U_p)x + \overline{W}x = \alpha_1(O.\mathrm{degPts}\,0\,x)$ for all $x \in J_H$.
--
--   *The Serre dlog export.* $\Theta_0$ is an additive map from the $p$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}},$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`$)$ to $\Omega_{\mathrm{ss}}$, and $\Psi$ a map from the same torsion subgroup to `qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ'`, subject to: `hrec`: $\Theta_0 x = (\Psi x)^{-1}\, d(\Psi x)$ in $\Omega[\cdot/K]$; `hPIN`: for each $x$ there are a degree-zero divisor $D$ with class $x$, a nonzero $f$ in the function field and a Laurent series $y$ over `Pl` such that $p\,(\mathrm{wgen}\cdot D)(v) = \mathrm{ord}_v f$ for every place $v$, the Laurent expansion of $f$ is the image of $y$ under the inclusion of `Pl`, the reduction of $y$ to the residue field is nonzero, and the Laurent series of $\Psi x$ is the image of $y$ under reduction followed by the structure map to $K$; `hMULT`: $\Psi(x + x') = c\,g^p\,\Psi x\,\Psi x'$ for some $c \in K^\times$ and some $g$; `hNZ`: $\Psi x \neq 0$; `hORD`: $p \mid \mathrm{ord}_v(\Psi x)$ at every place $v \notin$ `ssPlacesQExp K Γ' p`; `hFIN`: the class $x$ lies in `O.finPts p` if and only if $p \mid \mathrm{ord}_v(\Psi x)$ at every place in `ssPlacesQExp K Γ' p`; `hP5`: at every place of `ssPlacesQExp K Γ' p` the differential $\Theta_0 x$ has a simple residue lying in the image of $\mathbb{Z}/p$ in $K$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses, the conclusion is: for every $\omega \in \Omega_{\mathrm{ss}}$ which is logarithmic, that is, for which there exists a nonzero $f \in$ `qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ'` with $\omega = f^{-1}\, d f$ in $\Omega[\,$`qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ'`$\,\!/K]$, there exists an element $x$ of the $p$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}},$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`$)$ with $\Theta_0 x = \omega$. No membership of $x$ in `O.finPts p` and no regularity of $\omega$ is asserted or assumed.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of Serre's $\mathrm{dlog}$ description of the $p$-torsion of the Jacobian in terms of supersingular polar differentials on the curve of level $M/p$ in characteristic $p$: every logarithmic differential in the supersingular polar space is hit by $\Theta_0$ on the full $p$-torsion, with no restriction to the classes extending over the place `Pl`. It feeds the dimension count [`ModularCurve.pow_finrank_map_residue_range_corner_mul_ncard_finPts_eq_natCard_corner_of_abelJacobiPin_of_representsRelSubPicLevel_raynaud_bridgePins_noKTransport_bridgePins4_of_algEquiv`](thm.html#ModularCurve.pow_finrank_map_residue_range_corner_mul_ncard_finPts_eq_natCard_corner_of_abelJacobiPin_of_representsRelSubPicLevel_raynaud_bridgePins_noKTransport_bridgePins4_of_algEquiv), which compares the size of the ordinary corner of the Tate module with the residue space of the supersingular polar differentials.
